; The control for defn-sees-top-level-let.fk: the same shape one frame deeper.
; A `let` inside a defn body, read by a defn declared in that same body. Every
; kernel answers 5, so nothing about closing over a binding is itself the trouble.
;
; preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk
(do
    (defn outerfn ()
        (do (let inner 5)
            (defn readsit () inner)
            (readsit)))
    (outerfn))
